<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">San Juan, Puerto Rico</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">San Juan is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a>, on a bay on the island's north coast. Spanish settlers moved there from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caparra">Caparra</a> around 1521, and it grew into a heavily fortified port guarding the routes of the Spanish treasure fleets, with the fortress of El Morro. It remained the seat of Spanish government until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> took the island in 1898.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/san-juan-puerto-rico.jpg" alt="San Juan, Puerto Rico" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Farragutful · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2013_Old_San_Juan_01.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
